+/*
+ * Serialisation across regions.
+ *
+ * LV1 accepts one outstanding command per storage device, not per region.
+ * The device has one bounce buffer, one command tag and one interrupt, which
+ * all regions share, so only one request may be in flight for the device even
+ * though every region has its own request queue.
+ *
+ * That is enforced by allocating a single blk_mq_tag_set with a queue depth
+ * of one and creating every region queue from it.  All queues built from one
+ * tag set take their tags from the same bitmap, so the single tag is the
+ * device wide permit to use the bounce buffer.  A request holds it from
+ * blk_mq_start_request() until blk_mq_end_request(), which the interrupt
+ * handler calls only after the hypervisor command has completed and any read
+ * data has been copied out of the bounce buffer.  This is how SCSI serialises
+ * several LUNs behind a host with can_queue == 1.
